# Third-party and borrowed code

The About screen in Topo and in Womble is this file: the apps read it out of their own bundle and render it, so what a person sees credited is what is written here.

Every borrowed piece in a Topo bundle is named below with where it came from and what its licence is. Nothing under a copyleft licence held by somebody else ships inside a bundle unless its holders waive the conflict between that licence and the App Store's terms, as iSH's do: Topo is distributed through the App Store, and embedding such code without that waiver would make the whole app theirs to object to. The iSH fork is the one such piece. What is left is permissively licensed code, Sam's own code, which carries no terms between one project and the other, tools that run on the Mac that builds Topo and stay there, and what Topo downloads after it is installed.

The format is the whole contract with the apps: a heading beginning `## ` opens an entry, and the `Licence`, `Where` and `Use` lines under it are shown as they are written. Everything above the first heading is the note at the top of the screen.

## Daphne
Licence: Sam du Rose's own code, as Topo is; no licence terms apply between the two
Where: samdu/daphne-assistant, `clients/ios`
Use: The pattern of the counted audio resources in `Apps/Client/AudioSession.swift` (record claims on the audio session, screen claims on the idle timer, hold claims on the background), the audio session categories and options and the reason the Bluetooth wideband option is not taken, the one-gate-per-microphone rule in `Apps/Client/VoiceInput.swift`, the refusal to install a tap on a dead input format, the on-device ear in `Apps/Client/Ear.swift` (the FluidAudio session, the measured vocabulary configuration, the locked sample sink and the caption glance, from `BuddyEar.swift`), the on-device voice in `Apps/Client/Voice.swift` (the Pocket manager, its measured `.ane` placement and per-stage compute units, from `FluidPocketEngine`) and the frame-streamed play queue with its time-pitch unit in `Apps/Client/Speaker.swift` (from `VoiceQueue`), with the silence keeper that holds the process open behind the lock screen and its counted owners (from `AudioIO.holdAlive` and `startKeeper`, and the cap on a wait in `TurnController.holdThroughLock`) and the rebuild of the queue on an audio engine configuration change (from `VoiceQueue.rebuild`).

## Topo mascot engine
Licence: Sam du Rose's own code, as Topo is; no licence terms apply between the two
Where: samdu/experiments, `topo-mascot-swift/Sources/TopoMascot` at 91139e8, the Swift port of `topo-mascot-engine/topo-engine.js` at e93fe1f
Use: `Packages/TopoMascot`, unchanged from the experiment: the engine that draws Topo the octopus on the composer's glass in pixels from the model, the context and what the turn is doing. Its golden frames are digests the JavaScript engine rendered (`oracle/golden.mjs` in the same experiment).

## FluidAudio
Licence: Apache-2.0, © FluidInference; its own bundled pieces are fastcluster (BSD-3, © Daniel Müllner and Google), vbx (Apache-2.0) and the text-processing-rs xcframework (Apache-2.0, FluidInference)
Where: https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio, pinned to 0.15.7
Use: Runs Parakeet and Pocket TTS on the phone. For `Apps/Client/Ear.swift`: loads the CoreML models Topo has downloaded, decodes an utterance, and rescores the transcript against the vocabulary with its CTC keyword spotter. For `Apps/Client/Voice.swift`: loads the Pocket language pack Topo has downloaded and synthesises a sentence as a stream of 80 ms frames, every stage placed off the GPU. Linked into the iOS app only.

## Parakeet
Licence: CC-BY-4.0, © NVIDIA; the CoreML conversions are FluidInference's
Where: https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-coreml and https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-ctc-110m-coreml, from NVIDIA's parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 and parakeet-ctc-110m
Use: The speech-to-text model the ear runs (parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2, 442 MB) and the CTC model that spots the vocabulary in the audio (parakeet-ctc-110m, 98 MB). Not in the bundle: Topo downloads them into the app's Application Support on the first run and keeps them there.

## Pocket TTS
Licence: CC-BY-4.0, © Kyutai; the CoreML conversion is FluidInference's
Where: https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/pocket-tts-coreml, from https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts
Use: The text-to-speech model the voice runs (351 MB: the four bundles of the English pack that the Neural Engine placement loads, the constants and the tokenizer beside them, and the `eponine` speaker, one of the pack's stock voices). Not in the bundle: Topo downloads them into the app's Application Support on the first run and keeps them there.

