## libarchive
Licence: BSD-2-Clause, © Tim Kientzle and the libarchive contributors; a few files are also under a 3-clause UC Regents copyright, and archive_getdate.c is public domain
Where: https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive at fc6563f5130d8a7ee1fc27c0e55baef35119f26c, the iSH fork's `deps/libarchive` submodule
Use: Reads the rootfs tarball and the Alpine packages, and writes the one archive they are combined into (`topo_ish_combine`), for the fork's fakefs importer (`tools/fakefs.c`). Built by `scripts/build-ish.sh` with no crypto library and no XML reader, and linked into the iOS app with the fork.

## Alpine Linux minirootfs
Licence: Each package's own: chiefly BusyBox (GPL-2.0), musl (MIT), apk-tools (GPL-2.0) and the Alpine base files
Where: https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.22/releases/aarch64/alpine-minirootfs-3.22.6-aarch64.tar.gz, pinned by size and sha256 in `Apps/Topo/Resources/models.json`
Use: The guest's root filesystem (4 MB). Not in the bundle: Topo downloads it into the app's Application Support on the first run, checks it against the pinned digest, and makes a fakefs of it there with the fork's importer.

